From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 minimal — AON pinctrl + USB host VBUS (PM5)

Adds the AON/CPUS controllers and switches on the USB-A (J8) VBUS so a device
enumerates on the USB2.0 host path (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-usb2-clocks` and `arm64-dts-a733-add-usb2-ehci-ohci-phy`):

 - r_ccu @0x07010000 — the PRCM CCU (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-minimal-r-ccu`), providing the AON bus clocks.
 - r_pio @0x07025000 — the S_GPIO pin bank PL/PM. Base + geometry from the pin tables of the A733 user manual
   (PL @0x00 / 14 pins, PM @0x30 / 6 pins) match sun55i-a523-r exactly, so it is
   reused via the "allwinner,sun55i-a523-r-pinctrl" fallback — no new pinctrl
   code. It takes only its apb clock and is a plain GPIO controller (no
   interrupts): the sunxi pinctrl clock-count gate is debounce-only, so one
   clock + no interrupt-controller is a valid GPIO-output-only instance.
 - reg_usb_host_vbus — a fixed 5V regulator gated by PM5 = USB_HOST_EN
   (schematic p7:172 / p13:92; SGM2576 U10 switching VCC5V0_USB20). Held on so
   the CH334F hub powers J8 and the on-board WiFi/BT. This is the port-power that a
   `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-usb2-clocks` and `arm64-dts-a733-add-usb2-ehci-ohci-phy` cross-check flagged as missing.

Only PM5/J8 is driven: J8 (behind the hub off USB1) is the USB2 host proof port.
J4 (USB0-DRVVBUS/PL2) belongs to the deferred USB3 combo, J16 (USB0/OTG) has no
enable GPIO wired.

defconfig (build.sh): SUN60I_A733_R_CCU + PINCTRL_SUN55I_A523_R.

HW proof (stick enumerates + reads on J8) pending — compile/dtc-gated only.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-r-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 
@@ -497,6 +498,22 @@
 		regulator-always-on;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * VCC5V0_USB20 -> the CH334F hub (USB-A J8 + on-board WiFi/BT), switched by
+	 * SGM2576 U10 whose enable is USB_HOST_EN = PM5 (schematic p7:172 / p13:92).
+	 * Held on: the hub must be powered for J8 and the WiFi/BT module to work.
+	 * PM5 lives on the AON S_GPIO bank (r_pio), bank index 1 (PL=0, PM=1).
+	 */
+	reg_usb_host_vbus: regulator-usb-host-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "usb-host-vbus";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		gpio = <&r_pio 1 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
 	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		/* Fallback 1 GiB; the bootloader fixes up the real size. */
@@ -1110,5 +1127,59 @@
 			phy-names = "usb";
 			status = "okay";
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * AON / CPUS domain. The R-CCU (PRCM @0x07010000) provides the AON
+		 * bus clocks; the r_pio (S_GPIO @0x07025000) is the AON pin bank
+		 * PL/PM. Base + geometry from the pin tables of the A733 user manual (PL @0x00/14 pins, PM @0x30/
+		 * 6 pins) which matches the sun55i-a523-r pinctrl exactly -- same
+		 * register geometry too (both the D1 NEW_REG_LAYOUT: 0x30 bank stride,
+		 * mux @0x00, data @0x10, drive @0x14, pull @0x24), NOT the main pio's
+		 * 0x80 that forced patch `pinctrl-sunxi-add-A733-sun60iw2-minimal-pio` -- so reused via the fallback compatible,
+		 * no new pinctrl code. The a523-r driver is an interrupt-controller and
+		 * requires the per-bank EINT lines or it fails probe with -ENXIO (which
+		 * took the VBUS regulator down with it in the first HW boot). The A733
+		 * S_GPIO EINT GIC lines are SPI 198 (PL) + 200 (PM), verified against the
+		 * UM interrupt table (anchor = vector/4, since the OCR'd text shifts the
+		 * INTID column by one row): GPIOL_NS = vector 0x0398 = INTID 230 = SPI
+		 * 198, GPIOM_NS = vector 0x03A0 = INTID 232 = SPI 200. These are the
+		 * *non-secure* lines Linux receives; the _S secure lines (SPI 197/199)
+		 * belong to the secure world, not us. Not a blindly-copied vendor value
+		 * -- an earlier A523-copied IRQ bug taught us to anchor on the UM. Routed to the main GIC
+		 * (root interrupt-parent). We use only PM5 as a GPIO output (VBUS
+		 * enable); the EINT domain is set up but unused.
+		 *
+		 * Caveat: the a523-r driver sets io_bias_cfg_variant =
+		 * BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL, the 1-bit write that was proven
+		 * wrong for the A733's 2-bit POW_MOD_SEL. It stays dormant here because
+		 * no bank has a vcc-pX-supply: the dummy regulator has no ops and no
+		 * fixed_uV, so regulator_get_voltage() returns -EINVAL and set_io_bias
+		 * leaves at its uV < 0 branch. A PL/PM supply needs an A733 r-pinctrl
+		 * carrying the correct 2-bit variant -- that is `pinctrl-sunxi-add-a733-r-pinctrl`.
+		 */
+		r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07010000 0x0 0x250>;
+			clocks = <&osc24M>, <&osc32k>, <&iosc>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_200M>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_300M>;
+			clock-names = "hosc", "losc", "iosc",
+				      "pll-periph-200m", "pll-periph-300m";
+			#clock-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		r_pio: pinctrl@7025000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-pinctrl",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-r-pinctrl";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07025000 0x0 0x800>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 198 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 200 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_R_APB0>, <&osc24M>, <&osc32k>;
+			clock-names = "apb", "hosc", "losc";
+			gpio-controller;
+			#gpio-cells = <3>;
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
+		};
 	};
 };
